# Answer key for B6 t1_breadth.sql - set-returning and table functions, breadth.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: all earlier decisions, plus D-26..D-28 (decided 2026-10-03, not implemented).
# Every node is schema-qualified (D-25). S7's series has no source and no boundary; that
# absence is checked in the report, not expressible here.

expect dangling_reference TABLE(ANALYTICS.EXPLODE_PAYLOAD) | S10: a user-defined SRF's body is not in this analysis; declared, never guessed

@ 17 S1 unnest in FROM
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.channel_mix.channel derived
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.channel_mix.revenue identity
forbid filter staging.orders.tags -> mart.channel_mix | an SRF in FROM is structural, like a join (D-27)

@ 25 S2 CROSS JOIN LATERAL, element filtered
value staging.products.tags -> mart.channel_mix.channel derived
filter staging.products.tags -> mart.channel_mix
note The WHERE on the element is a filter on its array.

@ 35 S3 two arrays by position
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.kpi_rollup.level derived
value staging.orders.discount_code -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment derived
forbid value staging.orders.tags -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment derived | the arrays bind by position: b is the second array

@ 44 S4 ARRAY[] constructor
value staging.customers.country_code, staging.customers.segment -> mart.kpi_rollup.region derived

@ 52 S5 WITH ORDINALITY (D-26)
value staging.products.tags -> mart.top_customers.full_name derived
influence staging.products.tags -> mart.top_customers.position
forbid value staging.products.tags -> mart.top_customers.position derived | the ordinal is a position, not a value from the array (D-26)

@ 61 S6 ROWS FROM with ordinality
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.top_customers.region derived
value staging.orders.currency -> mart.top_customers.full_name derived
influence staging.orders.tags, staging.orders.currency -> mart.top_customers.position

@ 70 S7 a series of literals
value core.dim_warehouse.id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity

@ 79 S8 a series bounded by a column (D-28)
value core.dim_store.opened_on -> mart.sales_daily.sale_date derived
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.sales_daily.region identity

@ 88 S9 a series in the select list
value core.dim_warehouse.capacity -> mart.kpi_rollup.orders derived
value core.dim_warehouse.id -> mart.kpi_rollup.customers identity

@ 97 S10 a user-defined SRF with a column-definition list
forbid value staging.orders.payload -> mart.kpi_rollup.level derived | the routine's body is not visible: declared, not guessed
forbid value staging.orders.payload -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue derived | the routine's body is not visible: declared, not guessed

@ 105 S11 TABLESAMPLE
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
value staging.orders.id -> mart.channel_mix.orders identity
filter staging.orders.status -> mart.channel_mix

@ 114 S12 regexp_split_to_table
value staging.customers.email -> mart.kpi_rollup.country_code derived

@ 122 S13 string_to_table in FROM
value staging.customers.id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.revenue derived

@ 130 S14 an unaliased unnest
value staging.orders.tags -> mart.product_performance.category_name derived

@ 138 S15 unnest in the select list over a nested function
value staging.customers.id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.email -> mart.customer_summary.segment derived

@ 147 S16 an unnest whose output is never used (D-27)
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.sales_daily.gross_amount identity
forbid filter staging.orders.tags -> mart.sales_daily | an SRF in FROM is structural, like a join (D-27)
forbid influence staging.orders.tags -> mart.sales_daily.gross_amount | the unnest repeats rows but names no column (D-27)
